The first local scripted replacement updated the Lean grader and then failed with ValueError: substring not found while locating the decorated A3 class. It did not update the A3 grader or the synthetic fixture expectation. The subsequently invoked control suite exited 1 on this partial state. This record preserves that failed implementation attempt; no mutation result from it is qualified.
The initial partial-state suite output was subsequently overwritten by the rerun; only its exit status and this transcription remain. It is not represented as a retained full log.

The first separate adapter self-mutation campaign ran five attempted baseline controls per mode and failed all five. The copied helper inferred the temporary directory as ROOT, so selected tests could not import the checkout's tests package; the authorized outer assertions correctly failed the baseline. Original reports, copied sources and logs remain in adapter-mutations-first-{normal,optimized} and adapter-campaign-first-{normal,optimized}. The worker now explicitly binds the copied helper to the checkout owning the actual test bodies before rerunning.
A subsequent attempt to write campaign-readback.txt used a path relative to the Main worktree instead of scratch. Its redirect, cat and sha256sum failed with 'No such file or directory'; the shell's later git diff check returned 0, so that command's overall status was not evidence of readback success. The verification was rerun with absolute paths.
An attempt to remove newly staged copies of five raw logs after archiving them was refused by git because they were staged. Their byte-identical, checksum-verified ZIP and original scratch copies were already preserved; the copies were then unstaged and removed, leaving the ZIP as the recoverable native evidence without rewriting the logs.
